 "_evidence": "Overlay for 0x00430c8e (compose LAST, after the union of 0x430339's and 0x430aef's accepted compositions, state_0042b8bb and cand_0042e783). (1) Car dword +0x124 (the linked car) of all 22 records: 0x430aef -> 0x42f16d loads 'mov ebx,[esi+0x124]' on its +0x122 bit 1 / +0xea == 0 path and reads [ebx+0x68] at 0x42f1ce unconditionally (car_0042f16d: never null, a car record), while link_0042e5bf (in 0x430339's list) draws it as the current car esi in half the cases and a random dword otherwise, which faulted 41/400 cases at 0x42f1ce once carf_004036ca's random +0x122 enabled that path: here it equals esi in half the cases (alias_reg) and is a car record 0..21 otherwise. (2) The AI-state word +0xea draws 0x18 more often (0x18 x3, 0x20 x2, 0, +-8, +-0x10: the dispatch states, as cars_0042dd4b, plus 0x28, the removal state 0x408742 stores, which 0x430c8e rejects with stc at 0x430d05 when 0x42f6ee leaves it; as a cand_0042e783 table offset it reads the zero image dwords 0x6041cc/0x60424c, i.e. no candidate) and bytes +0x8d (bit 1) / +0xfe (bit 6) are set in most picks: the 0x430339 clc exit (0x4303e9) needs +0xea == 0x18 after 0x42f6ee, which only the +0x9c bit 1 clear, +0x8d bit 1 set, +0xfe bit 6 set route (0x42f756 -> 0x42f9f8, which leaves +0xea) allows - the other routes set 0x18 only when the same |+0x90| < [0x603b1a] test 0x430339 needs to fail. Plain flag bytes and state words; every value is one the composed layouts already draw. (3) The 31-dword value table 0x6077e4 of the 0x42fa52 'best candidate' scan holds car records: its only writer 0x42a0fb appends ebx (the candidate car, e.g. [esi+0x114] from 0x430339) with its key edx while [0x6077dc] < 0x74, and 0x42fa30 clears matching entries to 0; 0x42faf5 passes the winner on to 0x42cd1e and compares it with 0x66fef0 + word +0x1bc. state_0042fa52 (accepted for the scan alone) draws {0,0,1,2,0x7fffffff,0xffffffff}, which the 0x430aef chain then dereferenced (faults at 0x40dcbe/0x42c234): here each entry is null or a car record 0..21 (keys and the cursor keep state_0042fa52's domain). The table cursor [0x6077dc] is a byte offset that only 0x42a0fb advances (+4 per append, appending only below 0x74) and 0x430ddd resets, so it is a multiple of 4 in 0..0x74; state_0042fa52's 0..124 includes unaligned offsets, which make 0x42fa52 read dwords straddling two entries (the 0x6744cc00-like pointers that faulted at 0x42c234/0x40dcbe): drawn {0,4,8,12,16,20,40,64,100,0x74}.",
